"$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ -6 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A,$ $Σ,$ and $V$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the first column of $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=10$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=3.$ Therefore, the first column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ -6 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{30}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb9ef2be-f5d0-5af1-b53b-519b082df85b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb9ef2be-f5d0-5af1-b53b-519b082df85b" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb9ef2be-f5d0-5af1-b53b-519b082df85b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-56b85f54-1a37-5dc2-9478-38992ce73b70" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ccbf4601-fbd3-5e4c-9bb6-eec9935bc33c" "answer-e2f9897b-7522-534a-b37a-9b1e054f353b" "answer-5afeb808-2408-5544-91eb-6e8f26969b1c" "answer-497e502c-a710-5896-85f2-7c55ee60c5a2" "answer-56b85f54-1a37-5dc2-9478-38992ce73b70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id