tion of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=7$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=6.$ Therefore, the second column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57b6d338-830b-5ed8-8f0a-f64dd8753dcc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57b6d338-830b-5ed8-8f0a-f64dd8753dcc" :answer-field/id #uuid "57b6d338-830b-5ed8-8f0a-f64dd8753dcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3eb57cdc-06ed-5be6-a085-358bde4fb1c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5bb86930-f90d-5b12-90e9-e48a9d51a232" "answer-3eb57cdc-06ed-5be6-a085-358bde4fb1c4" "answer-f788dd4c-e41a-55fe-ab74-c1d4c2ae177a" "answer-0b06010d-965b-582a-8b2a-49ead930bd31" "answer-0f85dcb3-9485-53ae-ae8a-22f225ec6ba6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bb86930-f90d-5b12-90e9-e48a9d51a232" :answer/id #uuid "5bb86930-f90d-5b12-90e9-e48a9d51a232" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3eb57cdc-06ed-5be6-a085-358bde4fb1c4" :answer/id #uuid "3eb57cdc-06ed-5be6-a085-358bde4fb1c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f788dd4c-e41a-55fe-ab74-c1d4c2ae177a" :answer/id #uuid "f788dd4c-e41a-55fe-ab74-c1d4c2ae177a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b06010d-965b-582a-8b2a-49ead930bd31" :answer/id #uuid "0b06010d-965b-582a-8b2a-49ead930bd31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f85dcb3-9485-53ae-ae8a-22f225ec6ba6" :answer/id #uuid "0f85dcb3-9485-53ae-ae8a-22f225ec6ba6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2a2f1d5d-f0eb-595a-8c0e-cc29b31a1a50" :question/id #uuid "2a2f1d5d-f0eb-595a-8c0e-cc29b31a1a50" :question/math-academy-id "q-96321" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -9 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}97 & -72 \\\\ -72 & 97\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=13$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=5.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=169,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-169I & =[\\begin{aligned}97 & -72 \\\\ -72 & 97\\end{aligned}]-169[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-72 & -72 \\\\ -72 & -72\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-169I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-25I & =[\\begin{aligned}97 & -72 \\\\ -72 & 97\\end{aligned}]-25[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}72 & -72 \\\\ -72 & 72\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-25I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f6f3e054-c4c5-504d-812f-3dc05a2404c5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6f3e054-c4c5-504d-812f-3dc05a2404c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f3e054-c4c5-504d-812f-3dc05a2404c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-79a6a184-7306-52e1-95cf-639b6b7e6197" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb9cd49c-9f1f-56ee-9533-c789a6678443" "answer-79a6a184-7306-52e1-95cf-639b6b7e6197" "answer-fad13cda-508e-5f38-8139-1c68904e8322" "answer-fcf93f69-7572-56fd-9cbf-709161a789c1" "answer-3a7a632d-1cf9-5bef-a9fc-f46a7da7ca7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb9cd49c-9f1f-56ee-9533-c789a6678443" :answer/id #uuid "cb9cd49c-9f1f-56ee-9533-c789a6678443" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79a6a184-7306-52e1-95cf-639b6b7e6197" :answer/id #uuid "79a6a184-7306-52e1-95cf-639b6b7e6197" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 